A||||3||Brian84SE||trunk ground wire||||1||
Z||000000||Brian84SE||10-14-2000||08:32 PM||||After putting my engine back together, there is just one wire I have left unattached.  It is the trunk lid ground wire.  Where does it attach to?  Does anybody have a pic?<BR>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||10-14-2000||08:34 PM||||Possibly the wire that attaches to the metal plate on underside of decklid. You will see a place dimpled where the wire attaches.||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||10-14-2000||10:45 PM||||if it is the thin black wire on the left side coming from the left deck lid support, it is a ground for the radio interference shield which is in the lower section of the deck lid when it is opened. You should see a black plastic clip to hold the wire and a raised connecting point on the left side of the shield where the end clip fastens.<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                         <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-15-2000||11:46 AM||||If you mean the wire is hanging from the lid... the other end goes to any solid ground point. usually the lower part of the hinge.||||reg||1
